INFO:__main__:{    "action": "Critical survival intervention required. Given the extreme environmental conditions with temperature at 46°C, complete ecosystem dormancy, and virtually zero resources, immediate actions are essential to prevent total physiological breakdown.    Strategic Survival Priorities:    1. Immediate Heat Management    - Seek absolute minimal rock overhang shelter    - Reduce body movement to conserve energy    - Position body in deepest shade possible    - Use any available cloth/material for head and neck protection    2. Emergency Hydration Strategy    - Carefully extract minimal water from river trickle    - Use improvised container for collection    - Purify through boiling if possible    - Consume water in extremely small, measured quantities    3. Energy Conservation    - Remain absolutely still during peak heat hours    - Minimize all physical exertion    - Control breathing to reduce internal heat generation    - Monitor body temperature to prevent critical heat stroke    Reasoning:    Current survival scenario presents near-catastrophic conditions. Body temperature at 39.8°C indicates imminent heat stroke risk. Water availability is critically low. Food is non-existent. Ecosystem has reached complete dormancy.    Survival depends on absolute precision in resource management and physiological control. Any miscalculation could result in fatal consequences."}
